 [F7] A connected manifold is path connected, locally path connected and semilocally simply connected by its ball and half-ball charts. It has a universal cover with free deck action of its fundamental group. [[thm-universal-cover-existence]] [[thm-deck-group-of-a-universal-cover-is-the-fundamental-group]]
 
+[F8] A compact smooth disk or arc can be put transverse to a finite family of smooth submanifolds by an arbitrarily small supported perturbation relative to its already transverse boundary collars. Apply this first in the boundary torus to a disk’s boundary arc and the other surface boundary circles, then in the interior to the disk and the other surfaces. [[lem-choice-free-relative-transversality-for-a-compact-smooth-embedding]]
